From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:52:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: link clicks the shell previews (Peek)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plan B49 (Peek, docs/arc-spec/06-flows.md §22): a plain click on a link
to another site in a favorite or pinned tab, and a Shift-click on a link
in any tab, must open the shell's preview panel instead of navigating the
tab or opening a window. The shell has to learn of the click before the
navigation happens, so the page stays as it was.

OACTab (OACLinkPreview) gets linkPreviewTriggers. The policy lives on the
WebContents (openarc::LinkPreviewPolicy):
- other-site clicks: a NavigationThrottle added by
  OpenArcContentBrowserClient::CreateThrottlesForNavigation cancels a
  user link click in the primary main frame whose registrable domain
  differs from the page's (CANCEL_AND_IGNORE: no request, no history
  entry, no error page) and reports it;
- Shift-clicks: OpenURLFromTab drops a renderer-initiated NEW_WINDOW
  link open with a user gesture and reports it.
The tab delegate hears of it through -tab:didInterceptLinkToURL:trigger:
(OACLinkPreviewDelegate) from a posted task. Tabs without triggers keep
the previous behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
